{"availability":"available","full":"oddcelot/vite-plugin-lit","name":"vite-plugin-lit","description":"This is a plugin to make Lit work with modern tooling featuring Vite and enabled HMR along side other nice things. ","category":"Developer tools","language":"TypeScript","stars":1,"forks":1,"created":"2026-09-16T20:49:29Z","updated":"2026-10-12T18:39:34Z","license":"BSD-3-Clause","branch":"main","homepage":"https://oddcelot.github.io/vite-plugin-lit/","topics":[],"demo":"https://oddcelot.github.io/vite-plugin-lit/start/demos/","color":"#25392f","ink":"#d1e5c5","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-13T07:36:37.961Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-13T07:36:37.961Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-13T07:36:37.961Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-09T22:06:47.245Z","stars":1,"forks":1},{"at":"2026-10-13T07:36:37.961Z","stars":1,"forks":1}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A Vite plugin for Lit projects with true HMR, CSS delivery helpers for shadow roots, and a DevTools timeline.","Started life in a fork of the lit monorepo as a proposed @lit-labs/vite-hmr package, and now lives here on its own. Lit is kept checked out as a read-only submodule for reference and opt-in canary testing against lit main.","lit-html decides \"is this the same template?\" by object identity of the TemplateStringsArray, not by content. Vite HMR re-executes an edited module, so a one-character edit rebuilds the component's entire subtree and takes focus, scroll, input state, and child @state with it."],"features":["Template-strings interning — the html/svg/mathml/css tags are","In-place class patching — the duplicate customElements.define from the","HMR that keeps state","Stylesheets at scale","Agent access — the same component tree and timeline"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/oddcelot/vite-plugin-lit/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"5187113bb039b21d5f3ffa603c764f4f3940c3acb97b4d6cc23bc47e73712e25","extractedAt":"2026-10-09T22:06:47.334Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T22:06:47